From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: media: h713-hdmirx: the ring is what the capture scaler writes, and INCAP moving on its own is a source change

Two faults of the same block, measured 12.10.2026 on the HY300PRO-G-EU
(1280x720 panel, arbeit/wurzeln-20261012, TODO 2.68 and 2.69).

1. The ring's size when the firmware scales was derived, not read: width =
   the pitch, height = source height * pitch / source width (0136f). For a
   1280x1024 source that gave 912x728, for 1360x768 1280x722 -- both taller
   than the panel, both refused by the display side, the console for two
   common PC modes. INCAP itself says what it writes: +0x86c is the capture
   scaler's output width, +0x870 its output height, and the slots' fill
   height agrees byte for byte (last written byte 656639 = 720 lines of
   912 for 1280x1024; 717.99 lines for 1366x768; 600 for 800x600):

     source      +0x86c  +0x870  rowbyte  +0x864 (factor)
     1920x1080     1280     720   0x50    0xaaaa = 720/1080
     1280x1024      900     720   0x39    0xb400 = 720/1024
     1024x768       960     720   0x3c    0xf000 = 720/768
     1360x768      1274     720   0x50
     1366x768      1280     718   0x50    (bounded by the width)
     800x600        800     600   0x32    (not scaled)

   So the ring is +0x86c x +0x870 whenever the pitch says the firmware
   scales, the pitch stays the rowbyte, and output words that do not agree
   with the rowbyte and the source (INCAP mid-change, its words move one
   after another) answer -ENOLCK instead of a guess. The DE scaler's input
   window, the former cross-check for the same information, goes: the
   firmware writes it only on a window-chain rebuild, and it read 1280x720
   while INCAP already captured 1280x1024. A board whose ring is the source
   (the HY310) takes the same path as before, byte for byte.

2. After a mode change the firmware's record names the new source at once,
   INCAP follows only when the capture chain is rebuilt -- seconds later at
   times -- and that step has no callback. A client that asked in between
   holds a ring nobody writes any more, and nothing tells it: with h713-warp
   streaming, INCAP read 1152x720 of the previous 1440x900 for a 720x480
   source through three SOURCE_CHANGE callbacks, moved to 720x480 without
   one, and the warp drew 1152x720 slots of a 720-byte ring until the next
   change (2 of 16 changes). The block is now looked at ten times a second;
   when active, rowbyte or scaler output differ from what the last detection
   saw, a SOURCE_CHANGE is queued. The client stops its queue and asks again,
   as for every other source change; the warp does so since the same day.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
@@ -253,25 +253,11 @@
 #define H713_INCAP_ROWBYTE_UNIT	16
 
 /*
- * The display engine's picture scaler at 0x05180000, and why it is only a
- * cross-check. Its input window, +0x34 (width [31:16], height [15:0]), is the
- * size the scaler reads the ring at -- 0x035401de = 852x478 on the HY300 Pro
- * for the case above, where the rowbyte says 864 = ALIGN(852, 16). It names
- * the ring exactly where the rowbyte can only name it to within 16 pixels.
- *
- * But the firmware writes it only when it rebuilds its window chain, which is
- * at the first lock of a boot and whenever the display side republishes the
- * VidDec descriptor (0117) -- not on every source change. Measured on the HY310,
- * 20.09.2026 (dev17): after 720p -> 1080p the window still read 1280x720 while
- * INCAP active and the rowbyte had long moved to 1920x1080 / 0x78. Taking that
- * register as the ring's size reported a 1280x720 ring with a 1920-byte pitch:
- * a sheared picture, then the console, not recoverable by replugging. So it is
- * consulted only after the rowbyte has said that the firmware scales, only
- * when what it says agrees with the rowbyte (ALIGN(width, 16) == pitch) and
- * with the source's aspect ratio, and only through an optional phandle: a
- * device tree without allwinner,scaler leaves the arithmetic alone in charge.
+ * The capture scaler's output size, +0x86c width and +0x870 height: what the
+ * firmware writes into the ring when it scales (h713_hdmirx_ring_geometry()).
  */
-#define H713_SCALER_IN_WIN	0x34
+#define H713_INCAP_OUT_W	0x86c
+#define H713_INCAP_OUT_H	0x870
 
